* **Status:** **PERMITTED**, subject to specific conditions:
1. **User Visibility:** The user must be informed that AI providers process their review text to generate drafted replies.
2. **No Model Training:** Third-party sub-processors must not use Google user data to train generalized AI/ML models.
3. **No Human Readability:** No employee or third-party human may read raw Google user data unless required for security, law, or explicit user request.



### 1b) Internal Dictionaries vs. Cross-Client Benchmarking

* **Source:** Google API Services User Data Policy — Limited Use Clause.
* **Confidence:** ✅ **HIGH**.
* **Internal/Per-Client Analytics:** **ALLOWED.** Using data to build non-generalized dictionaries, prompts, or client-specific trend reports directly serves the user feature requested.
* **Cross-Client Benchmarking / Aggregated Trends:** **ALLOWED ONLY UNDER STRICT CONDITIONS.** Google permits aggregated and anonymized derivations of data for internal operations or cross-client insights ONLY IF individual user/business data cannot be re-identified or extracted. You MUST NOT use raw Google data to train a global/generalized AI model that serves other clients.

### 1c) Required Wording for Privacy Policy

* **Source:** Google Developer Terms & OAuth Verification Requirements.
* **Confidence:** ✅ **HIGH**.
* **Exact Requirement:** Google explicitly requires the following exact clause or functional equivalent to appear verbatim in your Privacy Policy:

> *"VRYOH's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the [Google API Services User Data Policy](https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy), including the Limited Use requirements."*

### 1d) OAuth Scope Classification (`business.manage`) & Verification

* **Source:** Google OAuth 2.0 Scopes Directory & Verification Docs.
* **Confidence:** ✅ **HIGH** (Verified September/October 2026).
